Bosch eBike Live Data – Home Assistant add-on

The files bosch_ebike_ldi/app/bridge.py, livedata.py and ha_mqtt.py are
derived from possm/ha-bosch-ebike-pibridge
(https://github.com/possm/ha-bosch-ebike-pibridge, commit 82aa562, 2026-07-28),
licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE). Its LDI decoder was
itself ported from Xunil99/ha-bosch-ebike (MIT).

Changes made in this repository (marked "ADD-ON:" in bridge.py):

bridge.py
- Configuration read from Home Assistant add-on options instead of YAML.
- Adapter chosen by name (option "adapter") instead of first found.
- Shared-adapter safety: only devices exposing the Bosch LDI service are
  handled; other devices' disconnects are ignored and their bonds are never
  removed; bonded bikes are recognised at start-up from cached UUIDs.
- Pairing agent only accepts requests during the pairing window or from a
  known bike (upstream accepted every request), independent of the
  private_advertising setting.
- Adapter Discoverable is no longer set (it exposed classic Bluetooth; the LE
  advertisement has its own Discoverable flag). Adapter Pairable is only on
  during the pairing window and restored afterwards (upstream: on for good).
- A suspected stale bond is only logged; bonds are never removed
  automatically (upstream removed them after 3 failed connects). The pairing
  window no longer opens on every start (option open_pairing_on_start).
- Failure to become the default pairing agent is logged as an error.
- Device signals filtered by property name before any D-Bus call; the
  device address is read from BlueZ (not the object path), so bikes using
  random addresses keep one identity.
- Notification signal handlers are removed on disconnect (upstream added one
  per connection, so notifications were handled once per past connection).
- Signal subscriptions limited to BlueZ (bus_name).
- Re-advertising on adapter power-up, after a bluetoothd restart, and every
  5 minutes while a bike is missing (idea from Xunil99's ESP32 bridge).
  Bikes are marked offline when bluetoothd restarts or removes the device.
- Undocumented LDI fields are logged once each.
- Clear error messages when D-Bus or MQTT is unavailable.
- Pairing window length overridable via LDI_PAIRING_WINDOW_SEC (tests).

- "Forget paired bikes" handler, estimated remaining energy, last-seen time.

livedata.py
- ChargeEstimator takes an injectable clock (for tests).
- decode_live_data optionally reports undocumented fields.
- Light value 0 (invalid) decodes to None instead of False.
- New estimated_energy_wh().

ha_mqtt.py
- Bridge device labelled "Home Assistant add-on" (was "Raspberry Pi"), with
  the add-on version.
- Entity definitions as named tuples. Live-only entities use the bike's
  availability topic.
- Corrected labels and device classes: System Locked inverted for HA's lock
  class; Charger Connected (plug); Diagnostic Tool Connected; Light without
  the ambient-light class.
- Binary sensors render unknown for missing values.
- New entities: Estimated Remaining Energy, Last Seen, Forget paired bikes.

New files (our own): ble_policy.py, options.py, mcsp.py, protowire.py,
datapoints.py, datapoints.json, explorer.py, capture.py, add-on packaging,
scripts and tests.
